/-!
# Finite finitely presented approximations of integral algebra sheaves

Source: Stacks Project, Limits of Algebraic Spaces, Tag 082C(2),
lemma-integral-algebra-directed-colimit-finite
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-integral-algebra-fp-colimit).

The colimit universal property is in quasi-coherent commutative algebra sheaves.
The index is small in the section universe. No injectivity is imposed on any map.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- An integral quasi-coherent algebra on a qcqs algebraic space is a small nonempty
 directed colimit of finite, finitely presented quasi-coherent algebras.
Source: Stacks Project, Limits of Algebraic Spaces, Tag 082C(2),
lemma-integral-algebra-directed-colimit-finite
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-integral-algebra-fp-colimit).

Proof:
1. By lem-sfb-space-module-fp-directed-approximation and
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-category-directed-cofinal, write the underlying module of A
   as a directed colimit of finitely presented modules F_i. Form S_i = Sym(F_i),
   its maps to A and its functorial transitions, using
   lem-sfb-space-qcoh-affine-chart-calculus.
2. Let J_i be the kernel and B_i = S_i/J_i the image in A. The chart calculus gives
   quasi-coherence and the compatible transitions. On an affine etale chart, finite
   generators of F_i generate S_i as an algebra by
   lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-algebra-finite-presentation. Their images in A are integral,
   so lem-weil-pbc-finite-of-integral-generators makes B_i finite.
3. Every affine-chart section of A lifts through some F_i by
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-modules-elementwise, hence through B_i. Equality
   in A is equality in a common later image because B_i embeds in A. The chart
   calculus therefore makes the algebra-sheaf cocone B_i to A colimiting.
4. Approximate each J_i by a directed system of finitely presented modules E_ik.
   Let L_ik be the ideal generated by E_ik in S_i and Q_ik = S_i/L_ik. The chart
   calculus computes these ideals and quotients. The symmetric-algebra finite
   presentation theorem makes every Q_ik finitely presented as an algebra.
5. Order pairs (i,k) by i <= j and the condition that the transition sends L_ik
   into L_jl. By lem-sfb-space-fp-module-hom-colimit, maps E_ik to J_j factor at
   some stage E_jl. A common bound in the base followed by bounds in its row makes
   this preorder nonempty directed. The induced quotient maps satisfy the system
   laws since the quotient projections are epimorphisms.
6. In each row the union of L_ik is J_i, by the elementwise module-colimit theorem.
   Thus its quotient cocone has colimit B_i on affine charts and globally by the
   chart calculus. The row maps commute with pair transitions, as can be checked
   after the quotient projections. Apply lem-weil-pbc-directed-pairs-colimit-transitivity
   and step 3 to obtain colimit A over all pairs.
7. Choose an affine surjective etale chart by lem-sfb-qc-space-affine-etale-atlas.
   Finitely many algebra generators of S_i satisfy monic equations in B_i. By
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-rings-zero, all these equations vanish in Q_ik for
   k beyond a common bound k_0(i). The integral-generators theorem makes those
   Q_ik finite on this chart. The chart calculus descends finiteness to X.
8. The pairs with k >= k_0(i) form a cofinal nonempty directed subpreorder: increase
   the row index after choosing any common bound. Restrict the colimit using
   lem-weil-pbc-colimit-initial-full-subcategory on opposite preorders, and use
   the directed-cofinal theorem to replace the preorder by a directed partial order.
   All retained algebras are finite and finitely presented. On the empty space the
   chart is Spec of the zero ring, and no nonzero generators or relations are needed. -/
theorem exists_finite_finitePresentation_directed_colimit
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (X : AlgebraicSpace S)
    [CompactSpace (Point X.obj.obj)] (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated X)
    (A : X.QCAlg) (hA : A.obj.IsIntegral) :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder I) (_ : Nonempty I) (_ : IsDirected I (· ≤ ·))
      (D : I ⥤ X.QCAlg),
      (∀ i : I, (D.obj i).obj.IsFinite ∧ (D.obj i).obj.IsFinitePresentation) ∧
        ∃ ι : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj A,
          Nonempty (IsColimit (Cocone.mk A ι)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
